hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17954","Waki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The distinction between your fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal."
"17955","Waki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali ibn Rabah, that al-Lakhmi, narrated to us, from his father, he said, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, O Amr, fasten your weapons and your clothes and come to me. So I did and came to him while he was performing ablution. He looked me up and down and said, O Amr, I intend to send you on a mission, so Allah will keep you safe and grant you spoils, and I desire a good share of wealth for you. He said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, I did not become Muslim out of desire for wealth; I became Muslim out of desire for struggle and to be with you. He said, O Amr, excellent is good wealth for a righteous man."
"17956","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, Do not confuse for us the practice of our Prophet: the waiting period of the mother of a child when her master dies is four months and ten days."
"17957","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Shubah narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) openly, not secretly, say, The family of so-and-so are not my allies; my ally is only Allah and the righteous believers."
"17958","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said, I heard Dhakwan narrating from a freedman of Amr ibn al-As that he sent him to Ali to ask his permission to visit Asma bint Umays. So he gave him permission, until when he finished his need the freedman asked Amr about that. So he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, or forbade, to enter upon women without the permission of their husbands."
"17959","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Abu Qabil, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a thousand proverbs."
"17960","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, he said, I heard al-Hasan, he said, A man said to Amr ibn al-As, Do you see a man whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died loving, is he not a righteous man. He said, Yes. He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died loving you and employed you. So he said, He employed me, but by Allah I do not know whether it was love for me or seeking help through me. But I will tell you of two men whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died loving: Abd Allah ibn Masud and Ammar ibn Yasir."
"17961","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn al-Zubayr, he said, I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said, Amr ibn al-As used to visit us in turn. A man from Bakr ibn Wail said, If Quraysh do not stop, Allah will surely place this affair among a mass of the Arabs besides them. So Amr ibn al-As said, You lie. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, Quraysh are the rulers of people in good and evil until the Day of Resurrection."
"17962","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said, Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, narrated to us, from his father, he said, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, How far is your conduct from the conduct of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for him, he was the most abstinent of people in this world, and you are the most desirous of people for it."
"17963","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Musa, from his father, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, There was an alarm in Madinah, so I came upon Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, wrapped with his sword straps. So I took a sword and wrapped myself with its straps. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, O people, was your recourse not to Allah and to His Messenger. Then he said, Why did you not do as these two believing men did."
"17964","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Uthman, he said, Amr ibn al-As narrated to me, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me at the head of the army of Dhat al-Salasil. He said, So I came to him. He said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, who is dearest to you. He said, Aishah. He said, I said, Among men. He said, Her father then. He said, I said, Then who. He said, Umar. He said, Then he counted men."
"17965","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Amr ibn al-As, that he said, When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him in the year of Dhat al-Salasil, he said, I had a wet dream on a very cold night, and I feared if I washed I would perish. So I performed dry ablution then led my companions in the dawn prayer. He said, When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) I mentioned that to him. So he said, O Amr, did you lead your companions while in major impurity. He said, I said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I had a wet dream on a very cold night, and I feared if I washed I would perish, and I remembered the word of Allah Almighty: Do not kill yourselves; Allah is Merciful to you. So I performed dry ablution then prayed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said nothing."
"17966","Hasan narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, he said, Suwayd ibn Qays informed me, from Qays ibn Sumayy, that Amr ibn al-As said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, I pledge to you on condition that you forgive my past sins. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Islam wipes away what was before it, and emigration wipes away what was before it. Amr said, By Allah, I was the shyest of people before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I never filled my eyes with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nor questioned him about what I wanted, until he joined Allah Almighty, out of shyness before him."
"17967","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said, Rishdin narrated to us, Musa ibn Ali narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, A man said, O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best. He said, Faith in Allah and affirmation, and struggle in the path of Allah, and an accepted Hajj. The man said, You have said much, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Gentle speech, offering food, tolerance, and good character. The man said, I want one word. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, Go and do not suspect Allah concerning yourself."
"17968","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu Hani say, I heard Ali ibn Rabah say, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, while on the pulpit to the people, How far is your conduct from the conduct of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for him, he was the most abstinent of people in this world, and you are the most desirous of people for it."
"17969","Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr, from Amr ibn al-As, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, When the judge judges and strives then is correct, he has two rewards. And when he judges and strives then errs, he has one reward."
"17970","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ali ibn Rabah, he said, I heard Amr ibn al-As say, Morning and evening you desire what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) abstained from. Morning and evening you desire this world, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) abstained from it. By Allah, no night of his life passed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but what he owed was more than what he owned. He said, Some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowing. He said, And another besides Yahya said, By Allah, no three days of life passed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but what he owed was more than what he owned."
"17971","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu Qabil narrated to us, from Malik ibn Abd Allah, from Amr ibn al-As, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and elsewhere he said, Malik ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sought refuge from seven deaths: sudden death, the bite of a snake, a beast, drowning, burning, falling upon something or something falling upon him, and being killed while fleeing battle."
"17972","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Jafar, meaning al-Makhrami, narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, The Quran was revealed in seven modes; in whichever mode you recite you are correct, so do not dispute about it, for disputation about it is disbelief."
"17973","Abu Said narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, When the judge judges and strives and is correct, he has two rewards. And if he errs, he has one reward."
"17974","Yazid said, So I mentioned that to Abu Bakr ibn Hazm. So he said, Thus Abu Salamah narrated it to me from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet likewise."
"17975","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed us, he said, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had informed me, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Qays, freedman of Amr ibn al-As, he said, Amr ibn al-As heard a man reciting a verse of the Quran. So he said, Who taught it to you. He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me differently. So they went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said, O Messenger of Allah, such and such a verse, then recited it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Thus it was revealed. The other said, O Messenger of Allah, and recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said, Is it not so, O Messenger of Allah. He said, Thus it was revealed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, This Quran was revealed in seven modes; whichever of them you recite you have done well, and do not dispute about it, for disputation about it is disbelief, or a sign of disbelief."
"17976","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn Rashid al-Muradi, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, No people among whom usury appears but are seized by famine, and no people among whom bribes appear but are seized by fear."
"17977","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, he said, Amr ibn al-As asked permission to visit Fatimah, so she gave him permission. He said, Then Ali. They said, No. So he returned. Then he asked permission again, and said, Then Ali. They said, Yes. So he entered upon her. Ali said to him, What prevented you from entering when you did not find me here. He said, The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to enter upon women whose husbands are absent."
"17978","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, al-Faraj narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Amr ibn al-As, he said, Two disputants came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disputing. So he said to Amr, Judge between them, O Amr. So he said, You are more entitled to that than I, O Messenger of Allah. He said, Even so. He said, If I judge between them, what is for me. He said, If you judge between them and hit the right judgment, you have ten good deeds. And if you strive and err, you have one good deed."
"17979","Hashim narrated to us, he said, al-Faraj narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like, except that he said, If you strive and hit the right judgment, you have ten rewards. And if you strive and err, you have one reward."
"17980","Sulayman ibn Harb and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said, We were with Amr ibn al-As on a Hajj or Umrah, until when we were at Marr al-Zahran, a woman in her howdah had placed her hand on her howdah. He said, So he turned aside into the mountain pass, and we entered with him. He said, We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place, and there were many crows, among them a crow with a white belly and a red beak and legs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, None of the women will enter Paradise except like this crow among these crows. Hasan said, Then a woman with her bracelets and rings on her hands had placed her hands. And Hasan did not say, at Marr al-Zahran."
"17981","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shammasah, that Amr ibn al-As said, When Allah Almighty cast Islam into my heart, he said, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him, so he stretched his hand to me. So I said, I will not pledge to you, O Messenger of Allah, until you forgive my past sins. He said, So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, O Amr, do you not know that emigration wipes away prior sins. O Amr, do you not know that Islam wipes away prior sins."
